    <stix:STIX_Header>
        <stix:Title>AA22-321A StopRansomware Hive Ransomware</stix:Title>
        <stix:Package_Intent xsi:type="stixVocabs:PackageIntentVocab-1.0">Indicators</stix:Package_Intent>
        <stix:Description>On November 17, 2022, the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI), Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), and Department of Health and Human Services (HHS) released this joint Cyber Security Advisory (CSA) to provide information about known Hive Ransomware that has been identified through FBI investigations as recently as November 2022. 

This STIX file provides indicators of compromise (IOCs) associated with potentially malicious activity reported in CISA Joint Cybersecurity Advisory, AA22-321A #StopRansomware: Hive Ransomware."

The following URLs are anonymous file sharing sites, which are legitimate file hosting sites that are not inherently malicious, but were used by malicious actors to disclose victims’ data by utilizing their services. These URLs were not added to STIX content; however, it is recommended to monitor any connections to these URLs to determine if they are legitimate and deemed necessary for day-to-day operations within an organization: 
 
https://anonfiles.com
https://mega.nz
https://send.exploit.in
https://ufile.io
https://www.sendspace.com

Please be advised that some of the IP addresses listed are more than a year old, therefore, FBI and CISA recommend vetting or investigating these IP addresses prior to taking forward-looking action like blocking.
</stix:Description>
